  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation $(x+5)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=81?$",
  "worked_solution": "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =81 \\\\ (x-(-5))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-5,$ $b=3,$ and $r=9.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-5,3)$ and its radius is $9.$",
